Z||000054||Old Lar||07-21-2001||07:38 PM||||Songman:  That 66 Catalina was the best used car I ever bought (in 1967).  It needed to have the carburator rebuilt at 50K.  (my mother put some crap gas full of dirt in it).  Brakes (drum, drum) were every 20K miles or so.  Those full size 66's were the best looking of the Pontiacs in the 60's.  You could climb in under the hood to work on it.(of course, I was smaller then)  A 389 with a 2bbl even got decent milage (18 mpg over the road) in the age of $0.30 a gallon for premium.<BR>It was traded in 1972 and 90K miles later ($200 trade in value) for the 2nd worse car ever built.  A Vega GT wagon made from compressed rust.||||reg||1
